ntially [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0007]. Management's outlook language shifted from Hopper-driven demand to Blackwell, with the Q3 fiscal 2026 filing saying Blackwell architectures are the majority of Data Center revenue [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002]. The filings also flag H20 export licensing as a negative for future revenue [NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0002] and say data center, energy and capital availability could affect future revenue [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002]. Growth rates have decelerated from triple digits to 62% while absolute revenue keeps rising; the filings give no numeric forward revenue guidance.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "NVDA", "company": "NVIDIA Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Revenue was $60,922 million in fiscal 2024 (ended January 28, 2024), up 126% from $26,974 million in fiscal 2023, led by Data Center.", "citations": ["NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Revenue was $130,497 million in fiscal 2025 (ended January 26, 2025), up 114%, with Compute & Networking at $116,193 million, up 145%.", "citations": ["NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Q3 fiscal 2026 (ended October 26, 2025) revenue was $57.0 billion, up 62% year over year and up 22% sequentially; Data Center was $51.2 billion.", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0007"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Year-over-year quarterly growth moved from 262% in Q1 fiscal 2025 (ended April 28, 2024) to 94% in Q3 fiscal 2025 (ended October 27, 2024), 69% in Q1 fiscal 2026 (ended April 27, 2025), 56% in Q2 fiscal 2026 (ended July 27, 2025) and 62% in Q3 fiscal 2026.", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2024-04-28__mdna__0007", "NVDA_10Q_2024-10-27__mdna__0008"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The growth driver moved from Hopper (fiscal 2025) to Blackwell, now the majority of Data Center revenue in Q3 fiscal 2026, with a one-year product cadence.", "citations": ["NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0000", "NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Outlook risks stated: H20 export licensing requirements will negatively affect future revenue, and shortages of data centers, energy, or capital could impact future revenue.", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0002", "NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Period", "Revenue ($ millions)", "Year-over-year growth"], "rows": [["Fiscal 2024 (ended January 28, 2024)", "60,922 [facts:NVDA:Revenues:FY2024]", "126% [NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006]"], ["Fiscal 2025 (ended January 26, 2025)", "130,497 [facts:NVDA:Revenues:FY2025]", "114% [NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016]"], ["Q1 fiscal 2026 (ended April 27, 2025)", "44,062 [facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q1FY2026]", "69% [NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0006]"], ["Q2 fiscal 2026 (ended July 27, 2025)", "46,743 [facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q2FY2026]", "56% [NVDA_10Q_2025-07-27__mdna__0006]"], ["Q3 fiscal 2026 (ended October 26, 2025)", "57,006 [facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q3FY2026]", "62% [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0006]"]]}, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:FY2024", "claim": "Fiscal 2024 revenue", "quote": "60,922 USD millions"}, {"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:FY2025", "claim": "Fiscal 2025 revenue", "quote": "130,497 USD millions"}, {"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q1FY2026", "claim": "Q1 fiscal 2026 revenue", "quote": "44,062 USD millions"}, {"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q2FY2026", "claim": "Q2 fiscal 2026 revenue", "quote": "46,743 USD millions"}, {"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q3FY2026", "claim": "Q3 fiscal 2026 revenue", "quote": "57,006 USD millions"}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006", "claim": "Fiscal 2024 revenue up 126%", "quote": "Revenue | $ 60,922 | $ 26,974 | Up 126%"}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016", "claim": "Fiscal 2025 revenue up 114%", "quote": "Total | $ 130,497 | $ 60,922 | $ 69,575 | 114 | %"}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0000", "claim": "Hopper drove fi